#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f7h7.rst:5
#: 83ea0e86ff8245679e460f3782b50121
msgid "SLCAN Access on F7/H7 Based Autopilots"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f7h7.rst:7
#: 22696f249e7c4741b7b704e10fae7d10
msgid "Enabling SLCAN allows the autopilot to connect to CANBUS through USB on PC. It allows viewing, configuration and software updates of devices connected to the CANBUS. There are two different applications for using SLCAN to modify DroneCAN device parameters: DroneCAN GUI or Mission Planner. But first, the SLCAN interface must be enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f7h7.rst:11
#: e6fad1ff25284d06a6d02404f1726112
msgid "SLCAN access via COM port is disabled when armed to lower cpu load. Use SLCAN via MAVLink instead. The MAVLink method is generally preferred in any case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f7h7.rst:14
#: 73a9f440fdd147fa9b79d1dc1220ae7e
msgid "SLCAN Interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f7h7.rst:16
#: 57231dca12854384ade316ea742bbe07
msgid "The ArduPilot firmware provides two software USB interfaces, accessed simultaneously from the single physical USB connector. In  Mission Planner, you will see two COM ports assigned to the autopilot (if not, see Troubleshooting section below). One is for the SLCAN interface, the other for the normal MAVLink based Ground Control Station (GCS) connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f7h7.rst:18
#: ce33bb105e064910baa2b1ea134108f5
msgid "in firmware 4.5 and later, most autopilots that present two COM ports will both be for normal MAVLink connections and not have one default to SLCAN since SLCAN over MAVLink is the preferred connection method now."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f7h7.rst:20
#: 3e568c844b974fd4b27c76eedf984e33
msgid "In firmware 4.0 and earlier, they will be indistinguishable in the Mission Planner COM port selection box until you try to connect to the GCS with the SLCAN port that has been enabled for SLCAN protocol. (In later firmware versions, together with using the latest `Mission Planner driver set <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Tools/MissionPlanner/driver.msi>`__ , each port will be clearly labeled.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f7h7.rst:22
#: c086afbd0c154bb2b4b9a82598edfbd5
msgid "The port that will not connect (if already configured for SLCAN protocol, however, default is usually for MAVLink protocol so it can connect normally) is the SLCAN interface. This COM port is associated with a SERIALx port in the autopilot parameters. This SERIALx port will be the highest numbered port in the parameter list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f7h7.rst:24
#: 1b9833edc15f4f61a8d13fe0dd8a1da8
msgid "If both COM ports connect to Mission Planner, then the SLCAN protocol has not been set on that port and must be changed to use SLCAN."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f7h7.rst:27
#: 63a544b5febd4426bc59af69f3ac15a8
msgid "Configuring SLCAN SERIALx PORT"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f7h7.rst:29
#: 1a2335ae8b804e58a50cf01cd4d33fd9
msgid "Set CAN_SLCAN_CPORT = 1, if not already set or = 2 if you want to examine devices on a second CAN bus, if the autopilot provides it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f7h7.rst:31
#: 49890393109a47048dd3115c08409fc8
msgid "Connect to Mission Planner. In the Full Parameters list set the highest numbered ``SERIALx_PROTOCOL`` to 22 and reboot. Now only the non SLCAN USB COM port will connect to Mission Planner and the SLCAN port will be ready for use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f7h7.rst:35
#: 1f88a9b68ace47bdaccd769718b64451
msgid "Making Changes to DroneCAN Devices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f7h7.rst:37
#: 7c30438b4a474d5aa6b158716a09a275
msgid "Once SLCAN has been enabled, you can use :ref:`Mission Planner <planner:dronecan-uavcan-slcan>`  to make changes immediately to device parameters or firmware update."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f7h7.rst:39
#: a1165bdfd99e4c6bb214cff71b8a3c63
msgid ":ref:`DroneCAN GUI tool <common-uavcan-gui>` can also be used"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f7h7.rst:41
#: 592768d4219f4501b3b72a6d323f1cbd
msgid "here is an example video of configuring a DroneCAN power monitor device:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f7h7.rst:47
#: 1c4e5af8757148dfaeb92ca52a5930d5
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f7h7.rst:49
#: cc7ec4a336c5468f970141fc28102c02
msgid "Occasionally, Windows will only present one COM port in Mission Planner. In that case, you may still be able to connect to Mission Planner and change the parameters, if the COM port Windows has chosen to display is the autopilot port with MAVLink protocol selected.  However, you will most likely need to load the composite USB driver in order to obtain both COM ports, as shown in :ref:`these instructions<loading-composite-USB>`, once the SLCAN port protocol has been enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f7h7.rst:51
#: 711431e38f0143158d6576729e85834d
msgid "If you reboot the autopilot, the composite Windows USB driver may be unloaded and the process repeated upon re-attachment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-slcan-f7h7.rst:53
#: 19aa581905f44c71acbace2cad2290a8
msgid "If the SLCAN port has been configured, and if only one USB COM port appears, it may not be the normal MAVLink protocol port (usually SERIAL0) and you will not be able to connect Mission Planner. You can either re-enable the Composite Driver each time you attach, as above, or simply revert the SLCAN port to MAVLink protocol once attached with the Composite driver and subsequently use the single COM port Windows presents when connecting to Mission Planner."
msgstr ""
